      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Spanish settlers first established a permanent presence in the area in 1598, following earlier visits by Coronado's men in 1541.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cuyamungueinstitute.com/the-land/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the historic period, Cuyamungue’s inhabitants grew wheat and were introduced to fruit trees by the Spanish.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cuyamungueinstitute.com/the-land/history/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "After the Pueblo was abandoned around 1696, Spanish settlers claimed the land, and in 1699 a military officer secured a maize‑planting grant that included the old site.",
